WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.097 --> 00:00:02.751
(cheery music)

00:00:02.751 --> 00:00:04.837
- Okay, I'm Lois.

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.249
- And I'm Charlie.

00:00:06.249 --> 00:00:10.421
We have been told, and we
believe, that we have the largest

00:00:10.421 --> 00:00:14.346
private collection of
insects in the world.

00:00:14.346 --> 00:00:15.513
- [Lois] Yeah.

00:00:21.543 --> 00:00:23.498
(Lois laughing)

00:00:23.498 --> 00:00:27.500
- The story of how we met
was interesting enough.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.925
I was a teaching assistant
at the University of Arizona,

00:00:31.925 --> 00:00:36.535
and Lois was a student in the
class that I was teaching.

00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:39.000
We've been married for almost 55 years.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.246
- He's got a million
stories about insects,

00:00:41.246 --> 00:00:43.593
all of which I've heard,
and all of which I can

00:00:43.593 --> 00:00:45.288
fill in sentences.

00:00:45.288 --> 00:00:47.967
- And we've traveled
extensively, have been to all

00:00:47.967 --> 00:00:52.170
the continents, and 70
countries, collecting.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:56.309
It fills us with pleasure to
get into the field and collect,

00:00:56.309 --> 00:00:58.796
to spend the time in the field together.

00:00:58.796 --> 00:01:02.021
Oh, you need to look at the
antennae on one of these.

00:01:02.021 --> 00:01:04.522
It looks like a clown shoe.

00:01:04.522 --> 00:01:06.857
Well, I study weevils, and
the weevils are the largest

00:01:06.857 --> 00:01:09.108
family of living organisms.

00:01:09.108 --> 00:01:12.273
- These are plant hoppers, and
I think their noses are cute.

00:01:12.273 --> 00:01:15.331
I collect plant hoppers,
which are insects that feed

00:01:15.331 --> 00:01:19.125
on the juices of plants,
the phloem or the xylem.

00:01:19.125 --> 00:01:20.738
- With piercing, sucking mouth parts.

00:01:20.738 --> 00:01:24.602
- With piercing, sucking mouth parts.

00:01:24.602 --> 00:01:26.583
- Oh yeah, this is interesting.

00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:30.666
- When we get some insects
in, they're just dead.

00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:34.681
Of course we have to mount
them, so we have to pin them,

00:01:34.681 --> 00:01:38.553
or point them, and then we label them.

00:01:38.553 --> 00:01:42.137
Ah, the glue was not stiff
enough and he's falling

00:01:42.137 --> 00:01:44.061
off his point.

00:01:44.061 --> 00:01:47.886
Then, after I do that,
then I sort them to genus.

00:01:47.886 --> 00:01:51.977
- [Charlie] Each of these
units, trays, holds 55 specimens

00:01:51.977 --> 00:01:56.127
on average, and we have
at least a million weevils

00:01:56.127 --> 00:01:59.544
and a quarter of a million plant hoppers.

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:03.582
- Okay, here you come, darling.

00:02:03.582 --> 00:02:04.997
- [Charlie] We are donating the collection

00:02:04.997 --> 00:02:06.924
to Arizona State University.

00:02:06.924 --> 00:02:09.242
- [Lois] And there will
be research done on it,

00:02:09.242 --> 00:02:11.946
which is what we wanted to have happen.

00:02:11.946 --> 00:02:14.286
- [Charlie] When we were
entomologists at the university,

00:02:14.286 --> 00:02:17.275
we worked 14 hours a
day, seven days a week.

00:02:17.275 --> 00:02:19.860
Now we're down to eight
to ten hours a day,

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.974
seven days a week.

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:24.767
It's a lot of work, but we
both loved what we were doing

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:27.733
and sharing it was part of our life.

00:02:27.733 --> 00:02:30.313
- Now, which one do you
think is the prettiest?

00:02:30.313 --> 00:02:31.686
- [Charlie] These two.

00:02:31.686 --> 00:02:33.168
- I don't like that one.

00:02:33.168 --> 00:02:37.112
- Lois has often taken note of
the fact that a very large

00:02:37.112 --> 00:02:40.284
number of entomologists are divorced.

00:02:40.284 --> 00:02:43.256
- What I recommend is, if
you're going to be a taxonomist,

00:02:43.256 --> 00:02:45.952
a systematist, collect insects.

00:02:45.952 --> 00:02:49.785
You get a spouse that
is another entomologist.

